From 1150faabf332e9d5bd99b9df76103db5333aaa2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HampterDev <131729366+HampterDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:08:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Drop ESC-list entries for requests that leave no window

ui_window_mgr_make_window adds every tracked window ID to the ESC window
list before it looks for a factory, and ui_window_mgr_post_quit1 forgets
an ID only when it closes a window. A request that creates nothing
therefore leaves its ID in the list for good: no factory claims it
(0xd, 0xec), the factory finds nothing to show (pet info 0x58 without a
pet, homunculus 0x71, mercenary 0x7d), the request is refused (0x28),
or creation fails. Once such an ID is first in the list, ESC tries to
close it, fails and opens the ESC menu instead of cancelling active
navigation guidance. The 2022-04-06 executable updates the list the
same way.

After the request, forget the ID if no window resulted and none is
registered under it. Several factories return NULL for a window that
is already open (0xaa, 0xcb, 0xe5, 0x125, 0x132); those IDs are found by
ui_window_mgr_get_window and stay listed as before.

Validation: the new test_window_id_list runs the real
ui_window_mgr_make_window and ESC-list helpers with controlled
factories: unclaimed, empty, refused, untracked, back-of-list (0xcb),
already-open and stale-entry requests; it fails without the fix.
Release build without warnings; the full behavioral suite passed on the
completed series.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaQB81YtRGLtH8zvfX7WTY
